The documents under fixtures/public/ are anonymised derivatives (names, ids, text and fonts
removed by `xd redact`; geometry kept) of files from two open source projects. The exact upstream
files are pinned by commit and sha256 in scripts/fixtures.mjs; rebuild with `pnpm fixtures:build`.

  single      https://github.com/L2jLiga/xd2svg @ 937365e71fe735751053e918b3ba02cfa546ce7a
              test/input/single.xd       (MIT License, below)
  tests-suite https://github.com/AdobeXD/xd-to-flutter-plugin @ 16e22745ce9e9f67c2c6458be24420a8047be7be
              test_suite/tests_suite.xd  (BSD 2-Clause License, below)
  campvibes   https://github.com/AdobeXD/xd-to-flutter-plugin @ 16e22745ce9e9f67c2c6458be24420a8047be7be
              adobe_xd/example/Campvibes.xd (BSD 2-Clause License, below; "Campvibes" is a fictional
              brand drawn by Adobe for that example, and its name and every other text are removed)

The licences cover the files, not any third-party marks a design may contain; each file was chosen
because it is a generic template or a synthetic test document, and every node was rendered and checked
before it was added. A second file from the first project (multi.xd) is deliberately not redistributed.

